usb: dwc3: apple: set drvdata so remove() does not dereference NULL

dwc3_apple_probe() never calls platform_set_drvdata(), but
dwc3_apple_remove() starts with platform_get_drvdata() and immediately
takes appledwc->lock. Any unbind therefore faults on a NULL dwc3_apple:

  Unable to handle kernel NULL pointer dereference at 0000000000000560
  pc : mutex_lock+0x14/0x68
  lr : dwc3_apple_remove+0x24/0x78

remove() otherwise handles the DWC3_APPLE_PROBE_PENDING case explicitly,
so unbind is clearly meant to work. struct dwc3 is the first member of
struct dwc3_apple and to_dwc3_apple() is a container_of() on it, so the
dwc3 pointer is what remove() expects to get back.

--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-apple.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-apple.c
@@ -479,6 +479,8 @@
 	if (ret)
 		return dev_err_probe(&pdev->dev, ret, "Failed to setup role switch\n");
 
+	platform_set_drvdata(pdev, &appledwc->dwc);
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
